The Go rendering: a library whose exported API carries its enumerated types:
an interface method's parameter, a method promoted into an exported struct from
an internal type, a re-exported constant, exported constants of an unexported
type, an exported type with hidden members, an exported alias, slice and map
types, a method of an unexported type an exported function returns, and an
exported alias and a defined type of a pointer. One type is only compared
inside the library.

